Hi Zhichen,

This may or may not be your issue, as I’m just looking at this on my phone, but it seems that you have a problem right here:

>
> for (i in 1:I) {
>       if (sign[i] == 1){
>         we[i] <- a[i, 1]/a[i, 2]
>       }
>       if (sign[i] == 0){
>         we[i] <- 0
>       }

If you follow the brackets in your code, this part is still inside the n loop from above. Have you tried putting this section outside the n loop and running the code again? NIMBLE doesn’t like when the index on the left doesn’t include all the looping variables (so in this case, it may be expecting we[i,n]).

Hope that helps!

-Heather Gaya

