Thanks for posting the question, Michael. Thanks for checking it, Heather.
The example also works on my system.
It is hard for us to diagnose system-specific issues like this, but I can offer a few suggestions. You could try running R outside of RStudio to isolate if that causes a problem. Sometimes in the past we've had RStudio-specific issues, although not recently that I can remember. I doubt it's RStudio because Heather reported that it worked for her, but I thought I'd still note the idea. Next you could try updating/reinstalling XCode (and being sure to include command line tools). Sometimes you need to open it once to provide an authentication to compile stuff on your machine. Thinking specifically about why some (sounds like) system-specific compilation problem would arise from dmnorm in particular, maybe it has something to do with BLAS on your system? For the linear algebra in dmnorm, nimble's C++ library calls BLAS routines, which are included via R's math library. There is a note about this in section 4.5.3 of our User Manual, although it doesn't say much except to point you to R's documentation on BLAS. If you have your own BLAS installed, I wonder if that is somehow causing the problem.
HTH,
Perry

