hi Michael,

Sorry for the delay in responding.

When `dmnorm` is used in a model, behind the scenes the calculations are done using `dmnorm_chol`. So I wouldn't guess that changing your model code to explicitly use `dmnorm_chol` would solve the problem, but given it's unclear what is going on, it could be worth a try. You can't use `dmnorm_chol` directly in model code, so you'd need to write a user-defined distribution that invokes it (Perry's code in this thread is a good starting point). I'm happy to give more guidance on that if you run into problems.

I'm not sure what else to suggest. Before I noticed that your sessionInfo() shows you're using an Intel-based Mac, I was wondering if the issue might be arising on M1/M2-based Macs, but the example ran fine on my new M2 Mac, with R 4.3.2 linking to vecLib BLAS. And it ran fine on my older Intel-based Mac, linking to R's default BLAS.

-chris

