Hi Marwan,

As a first step, please take a look at these suggestions <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-mcmc.html#sec:initMCMC> for diagnosing initialization issues. A logProb of NA like this usually means that when the *prior* for, say, `z[1,9]` is being computed that there is an NA in one of the parameters of the prior, so it may simply be that you need to initialize other nodes in the model.

-chris

